# Milestone: M3
# Covers: stopping an outer tag terminates nested tag scopes; stopping an inner
#         tag leaves the outer scope running; echo traces enter/leave ordering.
# blocked: complex concurrent fixture; tag.stop() in parallel `,` strands needs chk step driver
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture calls t.stop() and u.stop() as urbiscript method calls on UTag
#   values — M4 object-method dispatch.  It also uses ',' (OP_FORK_DETACH) to
#   run f() concurrently while observing its output — M5 chk driver.  Nested
#   scope termination semantics with echo tracing require multi-strand scheduling.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag method dispatch and M5 chk driver):
# # var t = Tag.new() | var u = Tag.new() | function f() { ... } | {};
# # f(), sleep(100ms); ... t.stop() | u.stop(); ...
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/stop-depth.chk)
